Article 14 Where the contents recorded in an insurance contract are inconsistent, they shall be determined in accordance with the following rules:
(1) If the application form is inconsistent with the insurance policy or other insurance certificate, the application form shall prevail. However, if the inconsistency is explained by the insurer and agreed by the applicant, the contents recorded in the insurance policy or other insurance certificate signed for receipt by the applicant shall prevail;
(2) If non-standard clauses are inconsistent with standard clauses, the non-standard clauses shall prevail;
(3) If the times recorded in insurance certificates differ, the one formed later shall prevail;
(4) If an insurance certificate exists in both handwritten and printed forms, the content of the handwritten part signed or sealed by both parties shall prevail.
